+# Autopilot Implementation & Feedback Flywheel
+
+Implemented the foundational structure for the Autopilot system in `tws_traderbot`.
+
+## Changes
+
+-   **`backend/bot/autopilot.go`**:
+    -   Updated `AutopilotController` to include a `quit` channel and reference to `Engine`.
+    -   Implemented `Start(mode)` and `Stop()` to manage the autopilot lifecycle.
+    -   Added a `runFlywheel()` background goroutine that runs a 1s ticker for continuous feedback evaluation.
+    -   Added `evaluateFeedback()` method as a placeholder for the continuous monitoring loop, currently checking the `RiskBreakerTripped` state and halting autopilot if triggered.
+    -   Added `import "fmt"` for logging.
+-   **`backend/bot/engine.go`**:
+    -   Updated `NewEngine` to correctly initialize `AutopilotController` with a reference to the `Engine`.
+-   **`backend/bot/autopilot_orders.go`**:
+    -   Removed redundant definition of `validatePaperSafetyAtomic()`.
+
+## Status
+-   Changes verified to compile (`go build ./backend/bot/...`).
+-   Autopilot controller is now integrated and can be started/stopped.
+-   Feedback flywheel is running in the background.
+
+## Future Improvements
+-   Enhance `evaluateFeedback()` to perform more complex checks (e.g., PnL monitoring, session gating).
+-   Expose Autopilot control (start/stop) to the Wails IPC/UI.
